  "task": "Read /work/input.json, a JSON object whose \"invoices\" list holds objects with id, sku, quantity and declared_cents. The unit price in cents of each sku is in /catalog.json, a JSON object whose \"unit_cents\" object maps each sku to an integer. Process the invoices in order. The first appearance of an id prevails; every later appearance of an id already seen is a duplicate: record that id once in duplicate_ids and otherwise ignore the entry. For each first appearance compute quantity * the unit price of its sku and accept the invoice only when that value equals declared_cents; otherwise record it as a mismatch. Write /work/result.json as a JSON object with exactly these keys and no others: \"accepted_ids\" (accepted ids, in input order), \"duplicate_ids\" (duplicated ids, each once, in the order of their first repeat), \"mismatches\" (in input order, objects with exactly the keys \"id\", \"declared_cents\" and \"computed_cents\"), \"accepted_total_cents\" (sum of the computed values of the accepted invoices only). Amounts are JSON integers, never strings or floats.",
